import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors — design detail","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors — design detail","type":"design","date":"2026-10","refs":["ADR-0005"],"updated":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/design/0005-the-open-game.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/design/0005-the-open-game.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/design/0005-the-open-game.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-open-game-human-free-discovery-inside-anchored-anchors-—-design-detail" tabindex="-1">The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors — design detail <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-open-game-human-free-discovery-inside-anchored-anchors-—-design-detail" aria-label="Permalink to “The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors — design detail”">​</a></h1><p>Moved verbatim from ADR-0005 (ADR-0161 size budget). The ADR carries the rules; this page carries the context, tables, phases and trade-offs.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>ADR 0004 opened the move set: constructed objects — folds, bridges, carriers — are admissible <em>data</em>, not pre-approved Python. Since then the machinery closed a demonstrable loop: on <code>torch.export(ChunkedRetention)</code>, equality saturation under a guarded law set produces <code>decay</code>, <code>decay_vec</code>, and folded <code>applyd</code>/<code>aff_diag</code> carriers unaided; the scan tier lowers those carriers into real <code>triton.jit</code> kernels verified to ~1e-16 on CUDA; minted composites land in the cell store as <code>op</code> cells the registry walks uniformly.</p><p>The pressure this ADR answers: <strong>who authors the rules of play?</strong> Today the honest surface is threefold — the axiom the alphabet lacks (each missing structure was one guarded <code>R(...)</code>), the guard/derive predicates inside it, and the candidate enumerator. If those stay human, the system is an optimizer with a very good closure engine; it is not the optimizer that <em>discovers</em>. The question is which pieces of the game are anchors — things that cannot be self-minted without voiding the game — and which are merely <em>current capabilities</em>.</p><p>The measured boundary so far:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Closure is machine-owned.</strong> Given the vocabulary, the e-graph composes, folds, verifies, extracts, and lowers without naming anything — the RetNet recurrence is the existence proof.</p></li><li><p><strong>Invention is partially machine-owned.</strong> Composite ops mint today (<code>declare</code> emits <code>op</code>+<code>law</code>+<code>handle</code> cells); handlers mint (generated Triton runtimes); verified candidate equivalences mint (the compose sweep admits on a small space).</p></li><li><p><strong>Guards, enumeration, and derives are now partially machine-owned</strong> (updated 2026-10-15):</p><ul><li>guards synthesize — <code>auto_cond_object</code> mints the smallest declarative <code>cond</code> covering the measured-equal sites; the game&#39;s first <em>conditional</em> law (<code>xy + xz = x(y+z)</code> iff <code>x ≡ y</code>) came from it, not from a human;</li><li>candidates enumerate — <code>catopt_discovery.enumerate</code> instantiates 27 rewriting forms over the op grammar (1,160 candidates at depth ≤2, five paying laws auto-found), and <code>open_game</code> plays the stream as a board whose learned prior beats random on held-out pages;</li><li>derives synthesize — <code>dspec_synth</code> mints a declarative <code>dspec</code> from a procedural hook&#39;s measured outputs, refusing (with the missing bank op named) when the grammar cannot express it.</li></ul><p>What remains human is the <strong>form list</strong> (the 27 skeletons) and the <strong>mint target</strong> (which atom to propose) — one level up, planned as plan 0024. ADR 0004&#39;s standing lesson — direct law invention measured ~10× worse than structured construction — applies unchanged.</p></li><li><p><strong>The alphabet is open, not closed.</strong> A minted composite is new vocabulary; a declared op + generated kernel is an <em>invented atom</em> whose semantics is its code, verified observationally. The floor is substrate-expressibility, not the shipping op list.</p></li></ol><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p><strong>The optimizer is an open game: every rule, object, vocabulary, runtime, and pricing inside it is machine-made data admitted by anchored machinery — and the only fixed pieces are the substrate, the correctness oracle, and the clock.</strong></p><p>Concretely:</p><ol><li><strong>Three anchors, nothing else.</strong> (a) <em>The substrate</em> — torch, GPU, the Triton compiler; the machine cannot mint the thing it runs on. (b) <em>The correctness oracle</em> — observational equivalence of outputs on real tensors plus certificate replay; a machine that could redefine equivalence voids every certificate, so the checker is machinery, not mintable data. (c) <em>The measured objective</em> — wall-clock time and memory on the substrate; a self-minted objective is a rigged race. Everything else — laws, guards, ops, carriers, runtimes, cost models, the proposal grammar — is inside the game.</li><li><strong>The VM picture is already the architecture.</strong> Ops are machine <em>descriptions</em> (<code>op</code> cells); handlers are machine <em>instantiations</em> (<code>handle</code> cells); the codegen tiers emit the runtimes (generated kernels are small minted VMs); carriers are state machines (<code>applyd</code> = <code>h ← a⊙h+x</code>). A cost model is a handler into flop/byte space — therefore mintable; only the <em>measured</em> referee stays anchored.</li><li><strong>The alphabet stays open by construction.</strong> New vocabulary enters two ways: composites (closed-form — <code>decay_vec</code> = <code>pow(γ, arange)</code>, retractible as a <em>declared</em> atom) and declared-op/generated-kernel atoms (open-form — semantics is the emitted code, verified observationally). The residual floor is whatever the substrate cannot express — universal computation is in reach; silicon is not.</li><li><strong>The learned prior guides a verified search — RL does not replace it.</strong> The verifier is perfect (exact + observational, no fuzzy reward), the cell store gives curriculum, and imitation on claiming traces already warm-starts the policy. What RL does not fix: candidate density (~10⁹ law shapes, most invalid), cold start, and credit assignment across pattern + guard + derive. Guard synthesis is constraint-solving — conds are already data — not a policy problem. Quality-diversity beats raw RL for frontier coverage.</li><li><strong>The four dimensions hold at the meta level too.</strong> A synthesized law/guard/runtime is a <em>search</em> artifact that must pass the same semantics gate a shipped <code>R(...)</code> passes — numeric oracle → typed-pay gate → certificate replay → adversarial sweep of the guard&#39;s false region. Admission is never a vote the machine casts for itself.</li></ol><h2 id="the-categorical-spine-—-why-the-game-is-well-posed" tabindex="-1">The categorical spine — why the game is well-posed <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-categorical-spine-—-why-the-game-is-well-posed" aria-label="Permalink to “The categorical spine — why the game is well-posed”">​</a></h2><p>The ontology is the theory of <em>why</em> this architecture works; the machinery computes equational closure regardless. Its content:</p><ol><li><strong>Legality is derivable, not chosen.</strong> A move must be a structure-preserving map — folds, bridges, carriers are <em>homomorphisms</em>, the unique maps out of free structure. The proposer&#39;s space is defined by the algebra&#39;s shape, not a policy&#39;s imagination.</li><li><strong>Correctness is a formal object.</strong> Equivalence = same morphism in the semantic category; the e-graph is congruence closure — the free category modulo equations. A certificate is an algebraic proof the checker replays, not a heuristic.</li><li><strong>Engine-genericity is interpretation-as-functor.</strong> Evaluate, cost, verify, lower are <em>the same fold to different target algebras</em> — one traversal, four purposes. The four-dimension split (ADR 0003) is the consequence, not the choice.</li><li><strong>Chunking is a theorem, not a trick.</strong> <code>fold(concat x y) = fold x ◇ fold y</code> — the scan monoid homomorphism — is <em>why</em> the derived RetNet recurrence is exact. The machine produced the fold; the theorem guarantees legality. No tensor-level optimizer can state this claim.</li><li><strong>Knowledge is structural, so it transfers.</strong> Laws are equations on morphisms; carriers are state-machine morphisms; costs are denotations into ℝ. A minted cell carries structure, not tensors — which is why admitted knowledge applies to the next model unchanged.</li></ol><p>The honest caveat: this is CT&#39;s shallow end — Lawvere theories, equational closure, monoidal structure. No 2-cells, no string-diagram machinery, and the code never invokes it. Its role: the language the theorems are written in — what the game may mint, what admission certifies, and the formal spine any publishable claim stands on.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>The repository shrinks to machinery + the declaration kernel.</strong> Per-architecture knowledge — axioms, carriers, bespoke handlers — migrates into generated cells; dead knowledge dies in the evidence store without deprecation. The codebase gets <em>fewer abstractions</em>, not none: one generic game replaces N hand-authored optimizations.</li><li><strong>The measured win is the phase-1 gate.</strong> Nothing is defensible until a minted carrier beats the incumbent on a real model. <strong>Passed (2026-10-15):</strong> on the spelled <code>ChunkedRetention</code> export at T=512, extraction prefers the derived chunked carrier (29.4M vs 39.1M FLOPs) and the end-to-end probe measures <strong>1.82–2.33×</strong> against the fused baseline (866–1113 µs vs 2018–2028 µs), fp64 max-abs ≈1.3e-8. Honest scope: the paying kernels are the decayed fused + elementwise ones; the scan kernels are correctly declined as unloweable. The K-way construct (<code>om_kway_laws</code>) then cut the extracted cost a further 4.4× (6.70M, fold depth 1→7), with the O(T·C) floor (~2.59M) approached but not reached — extraction still prefers the spelled cross form.</li><li><strong>Guard synthesis is the research bet.</strong> If proposer + constraint-synthesized guards produce non-trivial admissions at useful rates, the claim is real — <em>the rule set as a synthesized, measured, admitted object</em> is the novel contribution. If not, the system remains: humans write axioms, machines compute closure — a solid optimizer, not the vision.</li><li><strong>Honest scars carried forward</strong> (updated 2026-10-15; closed items struck through). <s>Post-saturation site binding</s> (closed — <code>leaf_env</code> travels harvest → handler → <code>profitable</code>, and a raising kernel now declines instead of aborting the sweep); <s><code>derive=</code>-as-data</s> (closed where the grammar reaches — <code>dspec_synth</code> mints specs from measured bindings, refusals naming the missing bank op); <s>candidate enumeration and the learned prior</s> (built — <code>enumerate</code> + <code>open_game</code>; the prior is now <strong>trained and baked</strong> and its ordering beats the cost-delta heuristic on held-out pages, AP 0.133 vs 0.045). <strong>Open:</strong> extraction prefers the <em>folded</em> carrier (the ~2.59M floor); the <strong>form list</strong> and the <strong>mint target</strong> are still human (plan 0024); the falsified naive-RL path — enumerated, not reopened.</li><li><strong>What this is not.</strong> Not RL solving search; not an LLM writing rewrites; not a new op list. It is a game whose fixed pieces are silicon, the oracle, and the clock — the claim is <em>human-free optimization discovery within a declared algebra</em>.</li></ul>`,17)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};